C	ines_intro	0	greet	Ines asks for help
X	editor	pos	x=40;y=40
N	greet						The ledger is gone. Sixty years of catches, and it walks off the pier in a single night. Will you help me find it?
O	lighthouse					Tell me about the old lighthouse.
O	pier_history					How old is this pier?
O	why_ledger					Why does one book matter so much?
O	promise					I will find it.
N	lighthouse		l	greet			Dark since the storm of the ninth. The lamp is still up there, waiting for someone stubborn enough to climb.
N	pier_history		l	greet			Older than the town. The first planks went down when my grandmother was a girl, and half of them are still under your boots.
N	why_ledger		l	greet			Every catch, every debt, every share of every boat. Without it the whole season is a rumor.
N	promise						Thank you. Ask around the pier first, someone always sees more than they let on.
C	gulls_hint	1	ask	The Gull Feeder points the way
N	ask						Careful where you step. They remember faces, these birds.
O	tell					Has anyone come past with a big leather book?
O	gulls					You feed them every morning?
O						Never mind.
N	tell				knows_otter		Old Salt Otter took it, down in the den under the boardwalk. He reads it like a bedtime story.
N	gulls		l				Every morning since the lighthouse went dark. Better company than most of this pier, and they never ask for change.
C	otter_trade	2	offer	The otter names his price
N	offer						The ledger? Fine reading. Five silver koi and it is yours, and no haggling.
O	handover	count.trade >= 5	od	otter_agreed;otter_traded		Here. Five silver koi, fresh off the line.
